  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "A capacitor of capacitance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn><mi>pF</mi></math> is charged by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> source. It is then connected to another uncharged identical capacitor. Electrostatic energy loss in the process is____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>nJ</mi></math>.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "125",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/43e121cf-d781-4e5a-8617-3a4286b0828f-image.png\" style=\"width: 170px; height: 143px;\" /></p><p>Initial charge on first capacitor will be,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>C</mi><mi>V</mi></math></p><p>As the second capacitor is identical to the first one, hence potential drop across both capacitor will be equal to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>.</p><p>Now, loss of energy,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>C</mi><msup><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>C</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>C</mi><msup><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mi>C</mi><msup><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mi>C</mi><msup><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>100</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>125</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>125</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>nJ</mi></math></p>",
